 - Fix/cleanup **incorrect char formatting**: e.g.; `"Berang�r"` -> `"Beranger"`; removed non-English hints.
 - Consolidated **long, unneeded, or unused comments** into [Long_Comments/](/Long_Comments/) and replaced them with short custom markers or files to keep code clean, lean, and readable. > ~500k characters reduced and still ongoing.
 - **BBAI logging is now XML-tunable:** BBAI AI-decision logging can now be enabled/disabled and adjusted through **SAS defines**, rather than editing and recompiling the DLL as in base AdvCiv. This is deemed valuable **not only for modders, but also for users** who can now view or generate `BBAI.log` files for review. Note: `LoggingEnabled=1` in `CivilizationIV.ini` is still required for Civ4 to write. This allowed for example to surgically identify and fix the root cause of a city not producing its first settler until ~T90 at normal game speed, which is way too late (`bWarPlan` was too aggressively gating settler production; now it only blocks settler production after early expansion has reached enough cities (inefficient at that point, better switch strategy)). Note: BBAI logs can be very long; for broad raw-log diagnosis, we usually give to an external LLM/AI such as ChatGPT the log file, as it is as of now agentic-token-free analysis (also good to give us a different point of view/review if needed).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5925+) **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings, player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-head-example).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5925+) **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-head-example).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5962+) **BBAI worker log split:** added separate worker and Work Boat / `UNITAI_WORKER_SEA` BBAI log-level defines so ordinary `SAS_BBAI_UNIT_LOG_LEVEL` can focus on non-worker unit behavior such as scrapping, army movement, and combat-unit decisions. Worker and worker-sea logs had become noisy enough to hide those unit decisions, and Work Boats use distinct logic from land workers, so they now have their own category as well.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6016+) **BBAI Settler log split:** added `SAS_BBAI_SETTLER_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT so Settlers and other units can be inspected independently. This notably covers city-site decisions and Settler movement, scouting, returns, and founding; FOUND as of now separately controls detailed city-site scoring calculations. This notably lets UNIT investigate other unit behavior without enabling the multi-megabyte first-city Settler traces needed for example for the Berlin, Karakorum, and Cuzco regression tests.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5980+) **Culture-victory BBAI diagnostics:** added a new dedicated `SAS_BBAI_CULTURE_LOG_LEVEL` notably for diagnosing premature, uneven, or wasteful AI culture investment without enabling broad player/city logs. It records for example culture-stage reasons, current/projected Legendary-city countdowns and rival ranking, competing victory progress, actual culture-slider decisions, per-city weights and production, and culture contributed by production processes and assigned specialists.
@@ -249,6 +249,7 @@ Note: cultural victory bullets as of now assume 3 legendary cities are required,
 - **Barbarians** no longer attempt **world wonders** (prevents hammer sinks). See [KI#3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#3---now-fixed-with-a-dll-patch-barbarians-cities-building-wonders-in-particular-now-fixed-ie-disabled-for-world-wonders).
 - Barbarians also tend to **target weaker rivals**, and may **raze cities** more than base AdvCiv/Civ4
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6006+) **New World barbarian aggression toggle:** preserve both the old (as of now removed in Base AdvCiv) and the new Base AdvCiv behaviors via the `SAS_AI_BARBARIAN_NEW_WORLD_EARLIER_ATTACK_ENABLE` SAS define: The default `1` as of now uses the newer city/population presence rule that can end the local peace period earlier; the old as of now disabled `0` restores the older peaceable population rule.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6019+) **Barbarian Workers no longer retreat to the city they are already inside:** When a Barbarian Worker had no useful job and was already safe in a Barbarian city, Base AdvCiv still ordered it to "retreat" to that same city every turn. This trapped it in a pointless retreat/wait loop. It now simply waits for one turn (or may be scrapped when allowed), then checks again for useful work. See [KI#175](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#175---fixed-base-advciv-bug-barbarian-workers-in-cvunitaiai_workermove-repeatedly-retreated-to-the-safe-owned-city-they-already-occupied).
 
 #### Diplomacy (AI)
 
